  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Thursday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: High temperatures throughout Northern\nand Central Nevada this afternoon will be around ten degrees below\nnormal for this time of year. A trough of low pressure will move \nsouthward into Southern California this afternoon and this \nevening. As a result, precipitation chances will decrease this \nafternoon, before ending this evening. Minimum apparent\ntemperatures in the coldest valleys of Northern and Central Nevada\nwill be in the teens tonight. \n\nA ridge of high pressure will build eastward across Northern \nNevada Saturday through Monday, resulting in a warming trend. By\nMonday afternoon, high temperatures in Northern and Central\nNevada will be near seasonal values. A trough of low pressure \nwill move eastward across Northern Nevada Monday evening through \nTuesday afternoon. Any precipitation associated with this \natmospheric disturbance will remain north of Interstate 80. Dry \nweather is expected Tuesday night through Thursday.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High forecast confidence\nregarding unseasonably cool conditions this afternoon. High\nforecast confidence in valley rain and mountain snow ending this\nevening. Moderate forecast confidence regarding a warming trend\nSaturday through Monday. Low forecast confidence in the\npossibility of valley rain and mountain snow in Northern Nevada\nMonday evening through Tuesday afternoon. No deviations from the\nNBM model output.",
